      dxHamartomaDescription: 'Uncommon (<1%) benign solid lesion, usually hypervascular with nonspecific appearance. A highly specific pattern is a homogeneous, hypervascular lesion seen only in the arterial phase (isodense/isointense on precontrast, portal venous, and delayed/excretory phases); outside of that pattern, diagnosis is often one of exclusion among other hypervascular solid lesions.',
